  {
   "key": "0x3BA",
   "name": "input status register 1",
   "aliases": [
    "status register 1",
    "03DA"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "2762-2783"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
     "lines": "54-101"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
     "lines": "139-145"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
     "lines": "223-225"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_draw.cpp",
     "lines": "4404-4416"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Input Status Register 1 is read-only, at address hex 03DA or 03BA.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2762-2763",
       "sha": "e19f8685b27717239862f829f42063d0becb27e134318f120fb1184ab7bafc06"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "bit 3",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A set VR, bit 3, indicates a vertical retrace interval.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2772-2775",
       "sha": "86f705d893b0d500808c9610d7ce34b5891e53b3769d5bf7f8e4dd3dff184826"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "bit 0",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A set DE, bit 0, indicates a horizontal or vertical retrace interval: the real-time status of the inverted display enable signal.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2776-2778",
       "sha": "126d083f1b610d26614da9ec83dab52fd18e545615927b6684e16f015c14bd18"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2b",
     "on": "bit 3",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "VR can be programmed, through the Vertical Retrace End register, to generate an interrupt at the start of the vertical retrace.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2772-2775",
       "sha": "86f705d893b0d500808c9610d7ce34b5891e53b3769d5bf7f8e4dd3dff184826"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The document notes that programs once used this bit to keep updates in the inactive intervals, a need the video subsystem is designed to eliminate.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2779-2783",
       "sha": "0ec84cc75c1ffd6085c1ec0034793ca8634adbbe8889d98f80ac4f862abc071a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "A read of 03BA or 03DA clears the attribute controller flip-flop and the Tandy one.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "54",
       "sha": "7c75ddb61b5f190572dbe5b800e35aa1513bc25cfd85d2061e42e571b76e63f7"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "66",
       "sha": "c273548d671e86b3ff43dad4ad8b04a397baa08634dfd67343adf9f525a13f5c"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "68-69",
       "sha": "5956b180a9413d97e8ccb5e630dc7c859b6ef7f29f9d1a6efde97f5c93110312"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "143-144",
       "sha": "f6b128532c78c9b2fc5ceab10647a81534a611947fcde0cca84c02f2502b1cf3"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With the 3DA lockout flag set, a read returns zero at once.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "60-61",
       "sha": "bda9fcdea39a29fea26a9cb7149b902cbb797c2ba94e0046cd8125baf9920fb6"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "On a Tseng ET3000 or ET4000 bit 7 carries the complement of bit 3, which the VGAKIT check reads.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "96-98",
       "sha": "d110c8d63abaf0993486805bf7f53c27825a97bbe2509f5352bdf9b5c4b7db84"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "104",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With render on demand, render-wait off, the screen not disabled and the attribute flip-flop clear, a polling read renders the screen up to the current point.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "63-66",
       "sha": "5faa365d240469cc1cb8773e55c6c654d5b40a3fcf53017ff6de1fd96d7ce1b5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "105",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "On the CGA, Tandy and other adapters a read handler is registered at 03DA.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "223-225",
       "sha": "2325942714b3ed92c5f7de630dd27f5066e4bbca49b6f98c6a93b3167d1d0343"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "106",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "The status read is registered at 03BA when bit 0 of the Miscellaneous Output register is clear and at 03DA when it is set.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "112-114",
       "sha": "8b7f26df6a631a6c3d30062606adc70cd8550e101a33f3176686a209b5f32f62"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "143-144",
       "sha": "f6b128532c78c9b2fc5ceab10647a81534a611947fcde0cca84c02f2502b1cf3"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "107",
     "on": "bit 3",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "2b",
     "text": "DOSBox-X sets the retrace trigger and status bit 7 when the Vertical Retrace End register allows it, and raises IRQ 9 on the EGA build only, no interrupt on VGA.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_draw.cpp",
       "lines": "4404-4410",
       "sha": "ab18f53fa5f6777b320b472dc057562257fd061e3e3162cee7677e7ad2818e80"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_draw.cpp",
       "lines": "4411-4416",
       "sha": "8f5d05dc4aa863f952ebb9326ca02de22e0540e65364550caae2b6b6e62b155b"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_misc.cpp",
       "lines": "196-197",
       "sha": "a216f21d399cb4d25f8c018764ca63ee930223d6c51e6ae5915f8e2b769be6bc"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
